Hi, S+ users, provided below is a summary of responses I got for the Box
plot questions. I got so many answers from so many wonderful people. Tony
Lee, Jim Pratt and Jason Corner  suggested  making groups for columns of
data. Daniel Erdwin and Sally Rodriguez divided a graph sheet using "mfrow"
command. Laura Chihara and Greg Snow explained how to rearrange columns in
drop down menu for a Box plot. Naomi Robbins used an Excel work sheet to
concatenate several column data to a single column and  group the column
data in another column. Robert Garret provided Splus help files. Greg Snow
suggested creating another 3 column data/ rearranging data in drop down
menu. I hope I list all the names who tried to help me. Sam Buttrey used a
very simple command. Answers from each person are as follows:

Tony Lee: t <- make.groups(DS3$V1 = "1",DS3$V2 = "2",DS3$V3 = "3")
bwplot(which~data, data=t)
Jim Pratt:
bwplot(c(col1,col2,col3)~rep(1:3,c(length(col1),length(col2),length(col3))))

        Jason Corner: >
boxplot(split(c(x,y,z),c(rep("x",length(x)),rep("y",length(y)),rep("z",lengt
h(z)))))
        Sally Rodriguez: par(mfrow=c(1,3)) boxplot(DATA[,1],ylab="Value from
data in Column 1",main="Plot of Variable 1")
        Daniel Erdwin: par(mfrow=c(1,3)) or par(mfrow=c(3,1)) then do box
plots independently one after each other.
Laura Chihara: select Data > Restructure > Stack On the From side, select
the Data Set: that holds the variables, select the variables you want
side-by-side boxplots of in the Stack Columns drop-down list, and make sure
Create Group Columns is checked. On the To: side, give a new name for a data
set, and enter names for the new columns you create (Stack Column and Group
Column fields).
         Greg Snow: > boxplot(fuel.frame) or for GUI, use the
Data>Restructure>Stack from the menus to create an new dataframe that is set
up the way the gui wants to see it
Naomi Robins: In the attached Excel file I converted three columns of data
(the worksheet labeled 3col) into one long column labeled "col 1", "col 2",
and "col 3".  
Sam Buttrey: boxplot (list (firstcol, secondcol, thirdcol)).
Robert Garret: Refer to help file

Original Question: 
Hi, S+ user, I'd like to create three box plots in one graph sheet. But I
can not use grouped box plot since I just want to compare three columns of
data instead of against categories as in the S+2000 book. I tried a
SHIFT-click method but it didn't work. Any other suggestion? I really
appreciate your help.

