From fharrell at virginia.edu  Wed Nov 15 23:39:05 2000
From: fharrell at virginia.edu (Frank E Harrell Jr)
Date: Wed, 15 Nov 2000 18:39:05 -0500
Subject: Summary: How to make tiny postscript files
Message-ID: <3A131E99.2459E1DF@virginia.edu>

Thanks to Patrick Connolly, Bill Dunlap, Max Kuhn, David Smith,
Don MacQueen, and Brian Ripley.  They pointed out among other
things using minimal margin and pointsize.  I used par(mar=rep(0,4))
but still got the errors.  I didn't realize though that a valid
file is still produced.  Oddly enough, using postscript(...,
pointsize=1) did away with the error messages (I have no text on
my graph) but resulted in a lot of wasted space in the image.

Max doesn't get errors when he uses another approach:
export.graph(Name = "GSD2",
   ExportType = "EPS",
   FileName = "C:\\TEMP\\small.EPS",
   Progressive = F,
   Height = ".5",
   Width = "2",
   Units = "Inch")
-- 
